    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully. The ASan output confirms exactly the bug I identified:\n\n- **Heap-buffer-overflow READ 4** at `stsz_box_read` in `box_code_base.c:5667`\n- The 8-byte allocation (2 samples × 4 bytes each) was overread at offset 8 (one past the end)\n- The crash trace matches: `stsz_box_read → gf_isom_box_read → ... → gf_isom_open_file → LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput`\n\nThe root cause: in `stsz_box_read`, when parsing a `stz2` box with `sampleSize=4`, the loop increments `i` by 2 (line 5660) before checking `ptr->sizes[i]` for max_size/total_size (line 5667). When `i` reaches `sampleCount`, this reads 4 bytes past the end of the allocated `sizes` array.",
